SPCX AVOID 2 | A core position needs a good business at an attractive price, and here the price cannot be tested at all. No multiple or fair value is computable, cash burn and dilution are getting worse, and there are only four months of trading history. Rising real yields add pressure. Conviction is 2, below the buy threshold of 4, so this is an AVOID with no position.
NVDA AVOID 3 | Quality is unmatched and own-history multiples are low, but those multiples rest on peak-cycle earnings with falling FCF conversion and concentrated customers. The price exceeds the bull fair value and the probability-weighted target sits below the close; a small macro tilt toward bear adds to it. Good but not compelling: AVOID, watch for a lower entry.
AVGO AVOID 3 | Quality is exceptional but the price embeds 41.7% growth and sits above even bull fair value. The probability-weighted 12-month value (~332) is below the price. Macro (real yields, spreads) tilts bearish, and AI-chip financing could add leverage. Good but not compelling: conviction 3 means no position. Revisit near P/E at its 5y median.
MCD AVOID 3 | Quality is excellent and the multiples are historically low, but the business is cheap for a reason. US comps are +0.8%, FCF conversion is falling, leverage sits at 3.60x while real yields rise, and the price is above the 218.53 base fair value. The probability-weighted upside is negligible. That makes the stock good but not compelling: conviction 3, so AVOID and hold cash.
